1226
01:05:00,875 --> 01:05:02,083
<i>Mapillai,</i> chana ready.

1227
01:05:02,166 --> 01:05:04,291
I will make hot chapatis.

1228
01:05:04,375 --> 01:05:06,375
Chinnu, how was the first day?

1229
01:05:08,250 --> 01:05:10,416
Viswanathan seems to be a very bad person.

1230
01:05:11,375 --> 01:05:13,166
He cheated me.

1231
01:05:50,875 --> 01:05:54,250
It's okay. This is also good in a way.

1232
01:05:54,333 --> 01:05:56,916
If you are at home,
take good care of the house.

1233
01:05:58,208 --> 01:05:59,083
Tell Chinnu.

1234
01:05:59,916 --> 01:06:01,083
Will you?

1235
01:06:03,750 --> 01:06:05,875
Yes, I will take care.

1236
01:06:07,416 --> 01:06:10,250
Water the plants in the afternoon
and in the evening.

1237
01:06:10,333 --> 01:06:12,291
Take Momos to the spa in the evening.

1238
01:06:12,375 --> 01:06:15,375
Tell Elan to sit behind and grab him.
Okay, Chinnu?

1239
01:06:15,458 --> 01:06:18,166
Don't go to the bathroom alone. Ask Elan.
He'll help.

1240
01:06:18,250 --> 01:06:19,291
Okay, Chinnu? Chinnu!

1241
01:06:19,375 --> 01:06:20,583
<i>…trapped</i>

1242
01:06:20,666 --> 01:06:23,416
Chinnu, you didn't say "I love you."

1243
01:06:23,500 --> 01:06:24,791
<i>No way to return</i>

1244
01:06:24,875 --> 01:06:25,750
I love you, Ammu.

1245
01:06:25,833 --> 01:06:32,291
<i>Trapped, trapped in a lion's den</i>
<i>While looking for a chicken piece</i>

1246
01:06:32,375 --> 01:06:37,125
Tank is overflowing. Switch it off.

1247
01:06:37,208 --> 01:06:38,083
Quickly.

1248
01:06:38,166 --> 01:06:41,833
<i>Went in search of</i>
<i>No honour, no pride</i>

1249
01:06:41,916 --> 01:06:47,333
<i>No shame, you ended up falling</i>
<i>Into the water when the booby trap was set</i>

1250
01:06:47,416 --> 01:06:50,250
Switch is here. Why did he run upstairs?

1251
01:06:50,333 --> 01:06:56,416
<i>No stamina, no breath</i>
<i>On Aadi Friday, choked, and fatigued</i>

1252
01:06:56,500 --> 01:07:01,916
<i>Idi idi idi idiyappam wife</i>
<i>Idi idi idi idiyappam wife</i>

1253
01:07:02,000 --> 01:07:05,333
<i>Idi idi idi idiyappam wife</i>

1254
01:07:05,416 --> 01:07:10,375
<i>Idi idi idi idiyappam wife</i>

1255
01:07:10,458 --> 01:07:15,208
<i>Mapillai,</i> please iron this top
and bring it quickly.

1256
01:07:24,541 --> 01:07:29,250
<i>Idiyappam! Everything has changed</i>
<i>You are the evidence</i>

1257
01:07:29,333 --> 01:07:32,833
<i>The whole town is talking</i>
<i>The new trend became viral</i>

1258
01:07:32,916 --> 01:07:36,375
<i>Amma became athai</i>
<i>The lion became a cat</i>

1259
01:07:36,458 --> 01:07:38,000
Job in Dubai…

1260
01:07:38,083 --> 01:07:39,541
<i>CSK Mumbai match</i>

1261
01:07:39,625 --> 01:07:41,250
<i>Started in the house</i>

1262
01:07:41,333 --> 01:07:42,166
Do this.

1263
01:07:45,583 --> 01:07:48,333
-Hey Momo. Momo.
-Feed it to him.

1264
01:07:48,416 --> 01:07:49,750
Switch on the TV.

1265
01:07:49,833 --> 01:07:50,708
<i>Idiyappam</i>

1266
01:07:50,791 --> 01:07:51,625
Hurry up.

1267
01:07:51,708 --> 01:07:54,041
It is so hot. Cool it a little and bring.

1268
01:07:54,125 --> 01:07:56,541
Come on, clean it properly.

1269
01:07:56,625 --> 01:08:01,625
<i>Idiyappam, idiyappam, idiyappam</i>

1270
01:08:01,708 --> 01:08:04,375
<i>Idiyappam, idiyappam, idiyappam</i>

1271
01:08:05,916 --> 01:08:09,291
-Is it okay, <i>athai?</i>
-No, do it again.

1272
01:08:10,500 --> 01:08:11,375
<i>Idiyappam</i>

1273
01:08:11,458 --> 01:08:15,250
<i>No life, no stamina, no breath</i>

1274
01:08:15,333 --> 01:08:18,916
<i>On Aadi Friday, choked, and fatigued</i>

1275
01:08:19,000 --> 01:08:20,458
<i>Idi idi idi idiyaappam wife…</i>

1276
01:08:20,541 --> 01:08:22,333
-Why are you sitting?
-I didn't sit.

1277
01:08:23,291 --> 01:08:24,166
Come quick.

1278
01:08:24,250 --> 01:08:25,125
Coming.

1279
01:08:25,916 --> 01:08:28,791
-Water ready?
-Where did you allow me to drink?

1280
01:08:28,875 --> 01:08:30,583
-Washed?
-How many times?

1281
01:08:30,666 --> 01:08:33,625
<i>Idi Idi Idi Idiyaappam</i>

1282
01:08:33,708 --> 01:08:36,083
Grocery list is there. Bag!

1283
01:08:36,166 --> 01:08:37,666
<i>Idiyappam</i>

1284
01:08:39,083 --> 01:08:40,333
-Bye, <i>athai.</i>
-Okay.

1285
01:08:40,416 --> 01:08:43,458
Uncle Murthy, let me know
if there's any good job in Dubai.

1286
01:08:43,541 --> 01:08:46,583
If there is a job in Dubai,
why am I here buying onions?

1287
01:08:47,125 --> 01:08:48,291
Who is in the shop?

1288
01:08:49,583 --> 01:08:50,750
Oh, you?

1289
01:08:51,541 --> 01:08:53,833
Okay. Pack everything in this list. Fast.

1290
01:08:53,916 --> 01:08:56,041
I have so much work to do.

1291
01:08:57,208 --> 01:08:58,583
Half a kilo of tur dal,

1292
01:08:58,666 --> 01:08:59,791
half a kilo of moong dal,

1293
01:08:59,875 --> 01:09:02,291
half a kilo of chana dal,

1294
01:09:02,375 --> 01:09:04,250
and two litres of oil.

1295
01:09:04,333 --> 01:09:06,041
Then sugar…

1296
01:09:06,125 --> 01:09:07,416
Half a kilo of that too?

1297
01:09:07,500 --> 01:09:08,416
Five hundred grams.

1298
01:09:08,500 --> 01:09:09,958
It's mentioned as 500 grams.

1299
01:09:10,041 --> 01:09:12,708
Then two Vim bars, ten eggs,
one packet of sesame seeds,

1300
01:09:12,791 --> 01:09:15,500
-and five kilo of rice.
-Rice means? Which one?

1301
01:09:15,583 --> 01:09:16,916
Which rice?

1302
01:09:17,000 --> 01:09:18,416
Give good quality rice.

1303
01:09:18,500 --> 01:09:22,125
Ponni, Deluxe Ponni, samai rice,
varagu rice, IR 8,

1304
01:09:22,208 --> 01:09:25,083
IR 20, kuthiraivali,
karuppu kavuni,

1305
01:09:25,166 --> 01:09:27,375
and so many other varieties.
Which one do you want?

1306
01:09:27,458 --> 01:09:29,250
Is there anything good
that you'd recommend?

1307
01:09:29,333 --> 01:09:31,583
What do you eat at home?

1308
01:09:31,666 --> 01:09:33,541
We will have biriyani at times.

1309
01:09:33,625 --> 01:09:35,291
Then, basmati rice.

1310
01:09:35,375 --> 01:09:37,125
Yes, yes. Same thing.

1311
01:09:37,208 --> 01:09:39,791
Why didn't you say this at the start?

1312
01:09:39,875 --> 01:09:41,458
Are you sure you want five kilos?

1313
01:09:42,333 --> 01:09:44,916
It is written as five kilos.
Give the same quantity.

1314
01:09:45,000 --> 01:09:47,375
Are you going to cheat by adding extra?

1315
01:09:55,458 --> 01:09:57,916
Look what your husband has done.

1316
01:09:58,000 --> 01:10:00,541
I asked him to buy regular rice,
but he bought biryani rice.

1317
01:10:00,625 --> 01:10:03,166
Are we eating biriyani three times a day?

1318
01:10:03,250 --> 01:10:07,000
If he wasn't sure, he could've
just called and asked, right?

1319
01:10:07,083 --> 01:10:09,125
-What, Chinnu?
-Leave it.

1320
01:10:09,208 --> 01:10:10,916
Don't worry, I'll handle it.

1321
01:10:11,833 --> 01:10:15,166
What? What are you staring at?

1322
01:10:15,250 --> 01:10:18,916
From now on, we'll be eating
this biryani rice three times a day.

1323
01:10:19,000 --> 01:10:22,000
No gravy. Just rasam.

1324
01:10:34,250 --> 01:10:35,583
Who is that?

1325
01:10:37,000 --> 01:10:37,958
Talk to me.

1326
01:10:38,041 --> 01:10:42,083
-One litre of imported liquor.
-Hey, where?

1327
01:10:42,166 --> 01:10:44,583
-In Vinoth <i>anna's</i> house.
-Hey, for me?

1328
01:10:44,666 --> 01:10:47,583
Hey! If you come before six o'clock,
you'll get it.

1329
01:10:48,083 --> 01:10:50,083
Otherwise, you'll only get
an empty bottle.

1330
01:10:50,166 --> 01:10:52,416
<i>-Come quick.</i>
<i>-Come quick.</i>

1331
01:10:52,500 --> 01:10:53,916
Starting right now.

1332
01:10:59,916 --> 01:11:02,750
<i>-Athai.</i>
<i>-I forgot to tell you.</i>

1333
01:11:02,833 --> 01:11:07,958
<i>In our area, they are giving 6,000 rupees</i>
<i>and two bed sheets for flood relief.</i>

1334
01:11:08,041 --> 01:11:10,708
<i>The ration card is on top of the fridge.</i>
<i>Green colour one.</i>

1335
01:11:10,791 --> 01:11:12,666
<i>Go quickly and get it.</i>

1336
01:11:12,750 --> 01:11:15,041
<i>Athai,</i> I'm going out.

1337
01:11:15,125 --> 01:11:17,208
<i>Do you think 6,000 rupees grows on trees?</i>

1338
01:11:17,291 --> 01:11:19,791
<i>Go get the money first, then you go.</i>

1339
01:11:19,875 --> 01:11:22,166
<i>Look, they'll give it only</i>
<i>until six o'clock.</i>

1340
01:11:22,250 --> 01:11:25,291
<i>Go and collect it.</i>
<i>I'll be there by seven.</i>

1341
01:11:30,500 --> 01:11:32,375
Boss! What is the bag for?

1342
01:11:32,458 --> 01:11:35,833
You will wrap the blanket around you
after getting?

1343
01:11:37,666 --> 01:11:40,416
Boss, can I stand before you?

1344
01:11:40,500 --> 01:11:42,125
-You want to stand before me?
-Yes!

1345
01:11:42,208 --> 01:11:44,791
Hey, get lost, man!
Why would I allow that?

1346
01:11:46,375 --> 01:11:49,416
Michael, I have started.
Do you hear traffic sound?

1347
01:11:49,500 --> 01:11:50,583
I'm coming now.

1348
01:11:50,666 --> 01:11:53,166
-Come. Otherwise it will be empty.
-Save some for me.

1349
01:11:55,750 --> 01:11:59,375
<i>Aaya,</i> it is getting late.
Can you get it for me?

1350
01:11:59,458 --> 01:12:02,833
Legs hurt standing since morning,
and you want me to get it for you?

1351
01:12:02,916 --> 01:12:04,625
-You useless fool!
-Okay. Go.

1352
01:12:04,708 --> 01:12:06,750
She is scolding me.
My <i>aaya</i> always talk sweetly.

1353
01:12:06,833 --> 01:12:08,541
I miss my <i>aaya.</i>

1354
01:12:08,625 --> 01:12:10,416
-You want to stand in front of me?
-No need.

1355
01:12:10,500 --> 01:12:11,833
For what joy, now?

1356
01:12:11,916 --> 01:12:12,833
RELIEF FUND
2026

1357
01:12:12,916 --> 01:12:14,416
-You are the last person?
-Take this.

1358
01:12:14,500 --> 01:12:15,750
-Hey!
-Go!

1359
01:12:15,833 --> 01:12:16,958
Take this, bro. Quickly.

1360
01:12:17,041 --> 01:12:18,541
It's getting late.

1361
01:12:18,625 --> 01:12:20,125
-Take this.
<i>-Anna?</i>

1362
01:12:20,208 --> 01:12:21,083
Take this.

1363
01:12:21,166 --> 01:12:23,500
Give this to the RCS Bank nearby.

1364
01:12:23,583 --> 01:12:25,958
-They will give.
<i>-Anna,</i> I don't understand.

1365
01:12:26,041 --> 01:12:29,583
Hey! You are supposed
to bring ration card, not ATM card!

1366
01:12:30,541 --> 01:12:31,708
Move aside.

1367
01:12:31,791 --> 01:12:33,000
Go. Go.

1368
01:12:33,083 --> 01:12:34,791
Please do something, bro.

1369
01:12:34,875 --> 01:12:37,583
My <i>athai</i> will knead me
like chapati dough. Please!

1370
01:12:37,666 --> 01:12:41,291
There's nothing I can do.
Write and collect it yourself.

1371
01:12:41,375 --> 01:12:42,541
Pick the phone.

1372
01:12:43,791 --> 01:12:45,791
Hey. I should call Vinoth <i>anna.</i>

1373
01:12:53,375 --> 01:12:54,458
Idea.

1374
01:12:54,541 --> 01:12:55,666
My precious.

1375
01:12:55,750 --> 01:12:57,958
-You remembered <i>aaya</i> just now?
<i>-It's not like that.</i>

1376
01:12:58,041 --> 01:12:59,583
<i>I raised you with so much love.</i>

1377
01:12:59,666 --> 01:13:01,958
<i>-Didn't you remember me?</i>
<i>-Aaya,</i> let me talk.

1378
01:13:02,041 --> 01:13:04,625
When you were little,
I'd sit beside you and roll kozhukattai…

1379
01:13:04,708 --> 01:13:06,291
-Let me talk.
<i>-…just the way you liked.</i>

1380
01:13:06,375 --> 01:13:08,125
<i>-You forgot all that.</i>
-Shut up!

1381
01:13:10,416 --> 01:13:13,041
I don't know what you'll do
or where you'll get it,

1382
01:13:13,125 --> 01:13:15,833
but somehow, please Google pay me
6,000 rupees, <i>aaya.</i>

1383
01:13:15,916 --> 01:13:17,333
<i>Let me see!</i>

1384
01:13:37,958 --> 01:13:39,416
You are not watching TV?

1385
01:13:39,500 --> 01:13:40,708
What?

1386
01:13:40,791 --> 01:13:42,666
Looks like the ration card
hasn't been touched.

1387
01:13:42,750 --> 01:13:43,916
Did you go or not?

1388
01:13:46,416 --> 01:13:47,833
I'm asking you only.

1389
01:13:47,916 --> 01:13:49,041
Did you go or not?

1390
01:13:58,625 --> 01:14:00,291
I went, <i>athai.</i>

1391
01:14:00,833 --> 01:14:02,875
I will Google Pay you.

1392
01:14:04,708 --> 01:14:05,875
Google Pay?

1393
01:14:06,708 --> 01:14:08,041
They won't do like that.

1394
01:14:08,916 --> 01:14:09,916
What, <i>athai?</i>

1395
01:14:10,000 --> 01:14:11,375
It is digital India.

1396
01:14:12,000 --> 01:14:13,333
Chandra!

1397
01:14:13,416 --> 01:14:15,625
It's cold. Please bring me a blanket.

1398
01:14:17,791 --> 01:14:19,916
Where are those two blankets?

1399
01:14:25,666 --> 01:14:28,750
You don't you know the difference between
an ATM card and a ration card?

1400
01:14:29,333 --> 01:14:30,625
Six thousand rupees gone.

1401
01:14:32,375 --> 01:14:35,083
It would have been useful
to buy food for Momos.

1402
01:14:36,375 --> 01:14:38,250
You are not responsible at all.

1403
01:14:39,416 --> 01:14:40,583
Sleep in the cold. Go!

1404
01:14:42,458 --> 01:14:43,416
<i>I jumped in blindly.</i>

1405
01:14:44,375 --> 01:14:46,291
Give me some idea, Vinoth <i>anna.</i>

1406
01:14:46,375 --> 01:14:47,250
I will tell you.

1407
01:14:47,750 --> 01:14:50,125
You know what some women usually do?

1408
01:14:50,208 --> 01:14:52,666
As soon as their husband
comes home from work,

1409
01:14:52,750 --> 01:14:55,916
they play both sides,
start complaining about his <i>amma.</i>

1410
01:14:56,000 --> 01:14:59,416
They'll not let him eat, sleep, or go to
work peacefully, pushing him into stress,

1411
01:14:59,500 --> 01:15:01,916
high BP, diabetes, and depression.

1412
01:15:02,000 --> 01:15:05,333
In the end, he either sends
his <i>amma</i> to an old-age home

1413
01:15:05,416 --> 01:15:07,375
or moves out to live separately.

1414
01:15:07,458 --> 01:15:08,541
Didn't understand?

1415
01:15:09,041 --> 01:15:10,666
Now, you are the girl.

1416
01:15:11,875 --> 01:15:13,791
Your wife is the husband.

1417
01:15:24,791 --> 01:15:28,166
Son, can you grind the coconut?

1418
01:15:28,250 --> 01:15:30,083
-Coconut, <i>athai?</i>
-Put it in the mixer.

1419
01:15:30,166 --> 01:15:31,000
Okay, <i>athai.</i>

1420
01:15:35,125 --> 01:15:37,583
Today I'm going to grind
this coconut in a way…

1421
01:15:45,291 --> 01:15:46,166
<i>-Athai?</i>
-Yes?

1422
01:15:46,250 --> 01:15:48,500
Why mixer is not working suddenly?

1423
01:15:48,583 --> 01:15:49,791
Oh, my God!

1424
01:15:49,875 --> 01:15:51,166
Don't know what happened?

1425
01:15:51,250 --> 01:15:52,541
-Mixer is not working?
-Yes.

1426
01:15:52,625 --> 01:15:54,375
Oh, my God.

1427
01:15:55,166 --> 01:15:57,458
She'll come and say, "I'm hungry."

1428
01:15:58,083 --> 01:16:00,541
My hands are covered in flour,
dear son.

1429
01:16:00,625 --> 01:16:02,708
Can you grind that coconut by hand?

1430
01:16:04,791 --> 01:16:06,041
What's the big deal, <i>athai?</i>

1431
01:16:06,125 --> 01:16:07,458
I will do it right now.

1432
01:16:07,541 --> 01:16:10,583
It's the grinding stone.
It's mother-in-law's grinding stone.

1433
01:16:19,916 --> 01:16:21,208
What happened?

1434
01:16:21,291 --> 01:16:22,166
Nothing…

1435
01:16:22,791 --> 01:16:26,291
I crushed my finger today
while grinding coconut on the stone.

1436
01:16:26,375 --> 01:16:27,250
Why?

1437
01:16:27,333 --> 01:16:28,750
Mixer is there, right?

1438
01:16:28,833 --> 01:16:31,708
Hey! Aunt said
you like it ground by hand, right

1439
01:16:32,625 --> 01:16:33,708
Did you like it, Ammu?

1440
01:16:45,250 --> 01:16:46,333
<i>Amma.</i>

1441
01:16:46,416 --> 01:16:49,000
I believe you asked him to grind
the coconut by hand yesterday.

1442
01:16:49,500 --> 01:16:50,333
Yes.

1443
01:16:50,916 --> 01:16:52,833
-Why?
-Mixer was not working.

1444
01:16:59,291 --> 01:17:00,791
<i>Atrocity</i>
<i>What happened?</i>

1445
01:17:35,083 --> 01:17:35,916
Chinnu.

1446
01:17:37,208 --> 01:17:38,583
-Chinnu.
-Ammu.

1447
01:17:38,666 --> 01:17:39,583
When did you come?

1448
01:17:39,666 --> 01:17:42,000
-Coffee!
-Keep it there. I will finish this first.

1449
01:17:42,083 --> 01:17:43,333
Thank God!

1450
01:17:43,416 --> 01:17:45,416
I was about to put this
in the washing machine.

1451
01:17:45,500 --> 01:17:46,583
Aunt said

1452
01:17:46,666 --> 01:17:48,833
this material
would get spoiled in the machine.

1453
01:17:50,500 --> 01:17:51,666
Give it to me.

1454
01:17:53,375 --> 01:17:55,541
Nothing will happen to this material.

1455
01:17:56,541 --> 01:17:58,500
-Then…
-Hey, leave it. Ammu.

1456
01:17:59,125 --> 01:18:00,791
Don't keep asking mother-in-law
about everything.

1457
01:18:00,875 --> 01:18:03,125
She might have forgotten and said that.

1458
01:18:03,208 --> 01:18:05,458
I'm thinking of it as exercise and do it.

1459
01:18:05,541 --> 01:18:09,125
One thump, thump, one hit.
One thump, thump, one hit.

1460
01:18:09,208 --> 01:18:11,166
Thump, thump, thump.

1461
01:18:11,250 --> 01:18:13,541
<i>Amma,</i> did you iron my clothes?

1462
01:18:14,833 --> 01:18:17,750
<i>Maapilai,</i> can you iron the clothes?

1463
01:18:17,833 --> 01:18:18,916
Okay, <i>athai.</i>

1464
01:18:22,416 --> 01:18:23,750
Ammu, two minutes.

1465
01:18:33,125 --> 01:18:34,333
<i>-Amma.</i>
-Yes?

1466
01:18:34,416 --> 01:18:35,458
This month's salary.

1467
01:18:35,541 --> 01:18:37,125
Okay, okay.

1468
01:18:42,541 --> 01:18:43,416
<i>Amma.</i>

1469
01:18:44,250 --> 01:18:46,750
I only asked Elan to help you.

1470
01:18:46,833 --> 01:18:48,916
Don't dump every chore on him.

1471
01:18:57,333 --> 01:18:59,958
It feels like he's slowly taking
my daughter away.

1472
01:19:01,166 --> 01:19:03,791
I'm scared he'll separate her

1473
01:19:03,875 --> 01:19:06,250
from me completely.

1474
01:19:06,333 --> 01:19:08,958
<i>Don't let that happen from the beginning.</i>

1475
01:19:09,041 --> 01:19:11,500
<i>Keep everything under your control.</i>

1476
01:19:12,208 --> 01:19:14,500
<i>I had a daughter-in-law once…</i>

1477
01:19:14,583 --> 01:19:19,250
<i>She always played a double game</i>
<i>and took my son away from me.</i>

1478
01:19:19,875 --> 01:19:22,458
<i>Now there's no one</i>
<i>even to make me a cup of coffee.</i>

1479
01:19:24,750 --> 01:19:30,041
<i>Listen, Chandra, if he takes one big step,</i>
<i>you take a bigger one.</i>

1480
01:19:30,125 --> 01:19:31,708
<i>Hope you understand.</i>

1481
01:19:34,250 --> 01:19:36,208
Pavi's mom! Pavi's mom!

1482
01:19:37,208 --> 01:19:39,000
What curry did you make today?

1483
01:19:40,375 --> 01:19:41,791
Tamarind curry.

1484
01:19:41,875 --> 01:19:43,500
Can you give a little for my daughter?

1485
01:19:46,166 --> 01:19:48,833
Hey, why don't I see you upstairs
these days?

1486
01:19:49,375 --> 01:19:51,875
I have enough work in the house, aunty.

1487
01:19:51,958 --> 01:19:55,541
You'll get bored staying at home.
Come upstairs once in a while.

1488
01:19:55,625 --> 01:19:57,458
We will chat while making papad.

1489
01:19:57,541 --> 01:19:58,708
-Okay, will come.
-Okay.

1490
01:20:00,250 --> 01:20:02,708
Did you put groundnut in it?

1491
01:20:03,625 --> 01:20:05,833
Yes, I did.

1492
01:20:05,916 --> 01:20:08,458
-It will be tasty, eat.
-Thanks, Pavi's mom<i>.</i> Bye.

1493
01:20:08,541 --> 01:20:11,000
-You should come to make papads, okay?
-Bye, bye.

1494
01:20:21,166 --> 01:20:22,000
One minute.

1495
01:20:33,250 --> 01:20:36,125
-Today I'm a doctor. You?
-Slippers.

1496
01:20:43,750 --> 01:20:47,250
What would have happened? What would
have happened? What happened?

1497
01:20:49,375 --> 01:20:51,083
It will be okay if she wakes up.

1498
01:20:59,208 --> 01:21:00,291
Ammu, I love you.

1499
01:21:02,916 --> 01:21:04,916
Aunty from the house above
came over yesterday?

1500
01:21:05,000 --> 01:21:06,833
Yes, I gave curry.

1501
01:21:08,583 --> 01:21:09,875
Don't you feel ashamed?

1502
01:21:09,958 --> 01:21:12,458
When that aunty came,
what dress were you wearing?

1503
01:21:18,041 --> 01:21:22,958
I have enough work in the house, aunty.

1504
01:21:25,833 --> 01:21:27,708
You were trying to look glamorous?

1505
01:21:28,541 --> 01:21:33,291
That aunty was flirting with you.
And you were chatting happily too?

1506
01:21:34,291 --> 01:21:36,125
My <i>amma</i> felt so embarrassed.

1507
01:21:42,416 --> 01:21:44,125
She invited to sundry papads, I believe?

1508
01:21:44,208 --> 01:21:45,791
Yes, she called.

1509
01:21:47,125 --> 01:21:48,125
Yuck!

1510
01:21:52,000 --> 01:21:55,833
<i>Atrocity, what happened?</i>

1511
01:21:58,583 --> 01:22:02,166
Where's the crow? It only shows up
when we dry papads.

1512
01:22:13,708 --> 01:22:16,583
Do you need the AC on
while you are in the bathroom?

1513
01:22:17,875 --> 01:22:20,083
Does money grow on trees?

1514
01:22:20,166 --> 01:22:22,791
Can't you even switch off the AC properly?

1515
01:22:22,875 --> 01:22:25,916
My <i>amma</i> calls and scolds me
while I'm at work.

1516
01:22:26,000 --> 01:22:28,458
What am I supposed to tell you?

1517
01:22:30,708 --> 01:22:33,083
I switch on the AC only at noon.

1518
01:22:33,166 --> 01:22:35,250
I switch it off by one o'clock.

1519
01:22:36,291 --> 01:22:38,041
I use it only because it's summer.

1520
01:22:38,125 --> 01:22:42,291
Do you know what your <i>amma</i> said? She asked
if my <i>appa</i> pays the AC bill.

1521
01:22:42,791 --> 01:22:44,333
Her problem isn't the AC.

1522
01:22:44,416 --> 01:22:47,291
She indirectly complains
that I'm living here for free.

1523
01:22:47,375 --> 01:22:49,458
Okay, okay. Don't cry.

1524
01:22:51,041 --> 01:22:52,125
Don't cry.

1525
01:22:52,208 --> 01:22:54,833
No! I can't say anything.

1526
01:22:54,916 --> 01:22:56,958
You start crying immediately.

1527
01:22:59,166 --> 01:23:01,666
{\an8}What's wrong if your husband
wakes up early?

1528
01:23:01,750 --> 01:23:05,166
{\an8}He'll wait until all the work is done,
then wake up.

1529
01:23:05,250 --> 01:23:07,541
{\an8}She expects me to wake up
when she thinks is right time to wake up.

1530
01:23:07,625 --> 01:23:10,958
{\an8}Why does it matter when I wake up?
I finish all the work on time.

1531
01:23:11,833 --> 01:23:13,458
{\an8}Who dries underwear in the living room?

1532
01:23:13,541 --> 01:23:15,000
{\an8}Guests were there too.

1533
01:23:15,791 --> 01:23:18,041
{\an8}Oh, dear! What kind of upbringing is this?

1534
01:23:18,125 --> 01:23:21,333
{\an8}I don't know what to do. That day
I went upstairs to dry my underwear,

1535
01:23:21,416 --> 01:23:25,583
{\an8}your mom glared at me
because the upstairs aunty was there.

1536
01:23:25,666 --> 01:23:27,125
{\an8}So I dried it downstairs.

1537
01:23:27,208 --> 01:23:31,083
{\an8}What should I do? Fine!
I won't wear underwear anymore.

1538
01:23:31,166 --> 01:23:33,291
{\an8}-Happy?
-Hey, hey. Yucky! Yucky!

1539
01:23:33,375 --> 01:23:35,750
{\an8}The washed clothes have been
on the sofa for three days.

1540
01:23:35,833 --> 01:23:37,833
{\an8}Should I fold them too?

1541
01:23:37,916 --> 01:23:41,875
{\an8}I've never told you this before.
I fold all the clothes.

1542
01:23:41,958 --> 01:23:44,958
{\an8}Then your <i>amma</i> comes,
says I folded them wrongly,

1543
01:23:45,041 --> 01:23:47,500
{\an8}and folds them again.
Then why should I fold them?

1544
01:23:47,583 --> 01:23:50,250
{\an8}He's always on the phone.

1545
01:23:50,333 --> 01:23:52,833
{\an8}How do we know
if he's talking to a boy or a girl?

1546
01:23:52,916 --> 01:23:54,458
{\an8}Does your <i>amma</i>
really think that badly?

1547
01:23:54,541 --> 01:23:56,500
{\an8}Here, Pavi. If you doubt me,
check it yourself.

1548
01:23:56,583 --> 01:23:58,291
{\an8}How long does it take
to enter a password?

1549
01:23:59,291 --> 01:24:02,916
You said your husband stays home all day.

1550
01:24:03,958 --> 01:24:07,041
If he's idle,
he'll keep overthinking.

1551
01:24:09,791 --> 01:24:12,291
Okay, I have an idea.

1552
01:24:13,083 --> 01:24:15,875
Give him some responsibilities.

1553
01:24:15,958 --> 01:24:18,291
Then he won't have time to fight.

1554
01:24:18,375 --> 01:24:20,958
-Shall we start? Ready.
-Hey.

1555
01:24:23,333 --> 01:24:26,875
Ammu! Do you know
what your <i>amma</i> did today?

1556
01:24:30,875 --> 01:24:33,250
Here's this month's salary.

1557
01:24:34,666 --> 01:24:36,500
I'll give it only to you from now on.

1558
01:24:37,500 --> 01:24:40,125
You're in charge
of everything now, Chinnu.

1559
01:24:41,500 --> 01:24:42,375
Happy, Chinnu?

1560
01:24:44,875 --> 01:24:46,416
If Ammu is happy, Chinnu is happy too.

1561
01:24:54,458 --> 01:24:56,375
Aren't you going to buy groceries?

1562
01:24:58,041 --> 01:24:59,750
-Sir.
-Hi.

1563
01:25:00,791 --> 01:25:03,166
Please check if everything
is correct. It looks correct.

1564
01:25:03,250 --> 01:25:04,875
-Thank you.
-Hello! Leaving without tips?

1565
01:25:04,958 --> 01:25:06,458
-Don't want?
-Thanks.

1566
01:25:06,541 --> 01:25:07,458
Thank you, madam.

1567
01:25:07,541 --> 01:25:12,083
<i>The expense is ten</i>
<i>While the income is eight</i>

1568
01:25:12,166 --> 01:25:16,625
Spend carefully.
The bill is important, okay?

1569
01:25:16,708 --> 01:25:19,208
For <i>athai,</i> the total is 8,000.

1570
01:25:19,291 --> 01:25:22,500
-What is it, Chinnu?
-Is this the costliest rice?

1571
01:25:22,583 --> 01:25:23,541
Then give that one.

1572
01:25:23,625 --> 01:25:28,291
This is fat-free for Momos.
And this one is sugar-free for you.

1573
01:25:28,375 --> 01:25:30,000
One, two, three, four… Take it.

1574
01:25:30,083 --> 01:25:32,666
Spend carefully.
The bill is important, okay?

1575
01:25:33,458 --> 01:25:36,458
Expense 1500, okay?

1576
01:25:36,541 --> 01:25:41,916
<i>The expense is ten</i>
<i>While the income is eight</i>

1577
01:25:51,125 --> 01:25:53,625
Hi, Ammu. My sweetheart.

1578
01:25:53,708 --> 01:25:58,000
<i>Our guy is going to smash it</i>
<i>Bumrah bowled a no-ball</i>

1579
01:25:58,083 --> 01:26:02,666
<i>Whose wheel did the bumper hit?</i>
<i>Didn't keep count, didn't count the cash</i>

1580
01:26:02,750 --> 01:26:04,125
<i>Yet a balance still exists</i>

1581
01:26:04,208 --> 01:26:05,416
What's this, son-in-law?

1582
01:26:05,500 --> 01:26:06,833
-Robotic vacuum cleaner.
-Meaning?

1583
01:26:06,916 --> 01:26:10,291
It's hard for <i>athai</i> to bend
and sweep, right? Go, go.

1584
01:26:10,375 --> 01:26:12,750
Go on. <i>Mama,</i> look! It's moving.

1585
01:26:13,625 --> 01:26:14,833
-Is it?
-Yes.

1586
01:26:16,583 --> 01:26:18,583
Hey. Sensor. Move.

1587
01:26:18,666 --> 01:26:20,708
What was your math score in Grade 10?

1588
01:26:21,500 --> 01:26:22,625
Ninety-seven.

1589
01:26:22,708 --> 01:26:23,875
What about 12th?

1590
01:26:24,583 --> 01:26:26,375
One ninety eight.

1591
01:26:26,458 --> 01:26:28,958
How much money
did I give you on the first?

1592
01:26:29,041 --> 01:26:30,333
Fifty thousand?

1593
01:26:30,958 --> 01:26:32,083
How much is left now?

1594
01:26:32,166 --> 01:26:33,333
Two thousand!

1595
01:26:34,625 --> 01:26:37,083
I gave you money for 30 days,

1596
01:26:37,166 --> 01:26:39,750
but you spent it in just 15 days.

1597
01:26:39,833 --> 01:26:41,708
What did all your education achieve?

1598
01:26:42,333 --> 01:26:44,458
You never said it is for 30 days, Ammu.

1599
01:26:46,000 --> 01:26:48,833
Now, you know why my <i>amma</i> scolds you?

1600
01:26:50,041 --> 01:26:52,333
You're always blaming my <i>amma.</i>

1601
01:26:52,416 --> 01:26:54,458
If you behaved properly,
why would she scold you?

1602
01:26:56,708 --> 01:26:59,541
What are we going to do for money
for the next 15 days?

1603
01:26:59,625 --> 01:27:00,875
We'll have to beg.

1604
01:27:02,375 --> 01:27:04,541
Go ahead. Beg and come.

1605
01:27:22,291 --> 01:27:24,666
Hey! <i>Chithha </i>has come. <i>Chithha </i>has come.

1606
01:27:24,750 --> 01:27:29,041
Dear! You've come.
Oh, dear, you've become so thin.

1607
01:27:29,125 --> 01:27:32,750
You got drenched in the rain too.
Look who has come home.

1608
01:27:32,833 --> 01:27:34,916
-How are you, son?
-I'm good.

1609
01:27:36,625 --> 01:27:39,083
Do you still have to
go back to that house?

1610
01:27:39,166 --> 01:27:40,708
Just stay here.

1611
01:27:41,750 --> 01:27:43,458
Starting again from beginning?

1612
01:27:43,541 --> 01:27:45,791
Can you help me or not?

1613
01:27:45,875 --> 01:27:47,791
You never listen to me anyway.

1614
01:27:47,875 --> 01:27:52,000
Sleep. I'll ask <i>Appa</i>
and get it for you. Okay?

1615
01:27:57,833 --> 01:27:59,916
Sleep. Sleep well.

1616
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:01,958
You never seem to worry about anything.

1617
01:28:02,625 --> 01:28:04,541
Your <i>amma</i> studied
only up to eighth grade.

1618
01:28:04,625 --> 01:28:06,708
Even she manages
the household expenses well.

1619
01:28:06,791 --> 01:28:08,541
You can't even do that?

1620
01:28:08,625 --> 01:28:10,750
You can't hold a proper job.

1621
01:28:10,833 --> 01:28:12,500
Yet you shamelessly ask for money.

1622
01:28:12,583 --> 01:28:16,208
I'm still paying your home loan
from my pension.

1623
01:28:16,291 --> 01:28:21,000
Find a decent job first,
then bring your wife home.

1624
01:28:21,541 --> 01:28:23,125
Otherwise, don't come.

1625
01:28:29,583 --> 01:28:33,291
<i>The person you are calling</i>
<i>has not replied. Please try again later.</i>

1626
01:29:05,000 --> 01:29:06,166
<i>Maapilai,</i>

1627
01:29:07,208 --> 01:29:10,375
I admitted Pavi to school
for the first time.

1628
01:29:10,875 --> 01:29:13,750
I came home and changed my shirt.

1629
01:29:13,833 --> 01:29:15,958
She came running behind me, out of breath.

1630
01:29:16,041 --> 01:29:17,500
It will be around two kilometres.

1631
01:29:17,583 --> 01:29:19,666
She must have chased my scooter.

1632
01:29:20,208 --> 01:29:23,750
But I never imagined
she'd run back after marriage too.

1633
01:29:24,875 --> 01:29:26,458
I thought her life was ruined.

1634
01:29:29,708 --> 01:29:31,541
But then you came to my house.

1635
01:29:33,041 --> 01:29:35,708
No other man would have done that.
You did.

1636
01:29:36,541 --> 01:29:37,583
I felt proud.

1637
01:29:38,375 --> 01:29:41,000
But why did you do it, son?

1638
01:29:43,875 --> 01:29:44,916
I don't know, <i>mama.</i>

1639
01:29:47,000 --> 01:29:48,541
I like Pavi very much.

1640
01:29:49,458 --> 01:29:51,083
What did I do, <i>mama?</i>

1641
01:29:52,333 --> 01:29:54,541
Everyone thinks I'm useless.

1642
01:29:57,416 --> 01:29:58,666
<i>Maapilai,</i>

1643
01:29:59,166 --> 01:30:02,166
knowingly or unknowingly,
you've chosen a difficult role.

1644
01:30:03,833 --> 01:30:05,166
For generations,

1645
01:30:05,250 --> 01:30:08,291
we've burdened women with marriage.

1646
01:30:09,625 --> 01:30:12,458
Feeding the children,
taking care of the husband,

1647
01:30:12,541 --> 01:30:15,958
looking after the elders
and meeting everyone's needs.

1648
01:30:17,250 --> 01:30:21,166
Doing all this,
they forget what they want.

1649
01:30:21,833 --> 01:30:22,958
How do we see it?

1650
01:30:23,791 --> 01:30:25,416
We say it's just their job. Housewife.

1651
01:30:27,166 --> 01:30:29,166
Did they marry a building?

1652
01:30:30,791 --> 01:30:34,333
There's a better name for it. Homemaker.

1653
01:30:34,416 --> 01:30:36,166
They are the ones who build a home.

1654
01:30:36,916 --> 01:30:39,583
You may achieve a lot outside,
but if there is no peace at home…

1655
01:30:40,208 --> 01:30:43,625
My <i>amma,</i> your <i>amma,</i> Pavi's <i>amma,</i>

1656
01:30:43,708 --> 01:30:45,791
they all do the same. How?

1657
01:30:46,375 --> 01:30:49,708
Selflessly. With love.

1658
01:30:51,833 --> 01:30:53,541
You have two choices.

1659
01:30:54,416 --> 01:30:56,791
Walk away and go back home.

1660
01:30:59,333 --> 01:31:01,000
Pavi will eventually return.

1661
01:31:01,583 --> 01:31:02,583
After all, she's a girl.

1662
01:31:03,708 --> 01:31:06,291
But there's another choice.

1663
01:31:06,375 --> 01:31:07,916
It's harder.

1664
01:31:09,500 --> 01:31:10,458
But if you choose it,

1665
01:31:11,708 --> 01:31:13,083
your decision will show you

1666
01:31:14,166 --> 01:31:16,958
who you really are.

1667
01:31:17,666 --> 01:31:19,125
Think about it.

1668
01:31:32,291 --> 01:31:34,458
I spoke in anger.

1669
01:31:36,500 --> 01:31:38,750
No matter how much we fight,

1670
01:31:39,416 --> 01:31:40,916
don't stop talking to me.

1671
01:31:43,125 --> 01:31:44,208
I can't bear that.

1672
01:31:45,000 --> 01:31:46,250
Sorry, Chinnu.

1673
01:31:53,125 --> 01:31:54,375
Tell me.

1674
01:31:54,458 --> 01:31:56,791
Vinoth <i>anna,</i>
it's time to show who I am.

1675
01:31:56,875 --> 01:32:00,333
Super. Super. Wait a second.

1676
01:32:00,416 --> 01:32:01,666
Tell me now.

1677
01:32:02,958 --> 01:32:04,916
Vinoth <i>anna!</i>

1678
01:32:05,833 --> 01:32:10,125
From now on, the way I take care of
my wife, <i>athai, mama, thatha,</i> and Momos,

1679
01:32:10,208 --> 01:32:13,750
wait and watch

1680
01:32:13,833 --> 01:32:17,125
how much they are going
to love me in return.

1681
01:32:17,208 --> 01:32:18,500
Hang up, Vinoth <i>anna.</i>

1682
01:32:24,375 --> 01:32:26,500
Such a nice friend!

1683
01:32:38,541 --> 01:32:40,416
<i>Athai</i>. Come, <i>athai.</i>

1684
01:32:41,250 --> 01:32:42,708
I picked it fresh this morning.

1685
01:32:54,291 --> 01:32:55,541
<i>Athai.</i>

1686
01:32:55,625 --> 01:32:57,250
Your favourite chicken soup.

1687
01:32:57,791 --> 01:32:59,166
Have it.

1688
01:33:10,333 --> 01:33:12,708
The last time I came here
was with my Lakshmi.

1689
01:33:15,250 --> 01:33:16,791
-Nadhars Grandpa?
-What?

1690
01:33:16,875 --> 01:33:17,875
Up for a smoke?

1691
01:33:19,125 --> 01:33:20,375
Here.

1692
01:33:20,458 --> 01:33:23,416
<i>I feel the love floating in the breeze</i>

1693
01:33:23,500 --> 01:33:26,416
<i>When I learned the meaning of my life</i>

1694
01:33:26,500 --> 01:33:27,708
Wow!

1695
01:33:27,791 --> 01:33:31,583
<i>I feel I'm newly born again</i>

1696
01:33:31,666 --> 01:33:35,083
<i>When drenched in love</i>

1697
01:33:35,166 --> 01:33:40,000
<i>When a bird finds his way back to his nest</i>

1698
01:33:40,083 --> 01:33:43,833
<i>Even the tiniest twig blooms</i>
<i>With beauty in that moment</i>

1699
01:33:43,916 --> 01:33:47,833
<i>I soar beyond the sky</i>

1700
01:33:48,875 --> 01:33:52,125
<i>I open my heart beyond myself…</i>

1701
01:33:53,500 --> 01:33:58,333
<i>I see the love in the air</i>

1702
01:33:58,416 --> 01:34:00,708
<i>When I learned the meaning of life</i>

1703
01:34:00,791 --> 01:34:02,291
<i>Appa,</i> here's your diabetic pill.

1704
01:34:02,375 --> 01:34:04,208
I already ate<i>.</i>
<i>Maapilai</i> gave it to me.

1705
01:34:04,291 --> 01:34:06,500
<i>I feel I'm newly born again</i>

1706
01:34:06,583 --> 01:34:10,291
<i>When drenched in love</i>

1707
01:34:17,625 --> 01:34:20,541
What? A no-ball now?
What's happening?

1708
01:34:20,625 --> 01:34:24,000
-Mother-in-law! Our team's batting.
-Then that's fine.

1709
01:34:24,875 --> 01:34:27,166
-I didn't know.
-It's a free hit.

1710
01:34:29,250 --> 01:34:30,583
Buddy.

1711
01:34:31,916 --> 01:34:33,125
Can I keep it here?

1712
01:34:33,208 --> 01:34:35,416
-Okay. I'm leaving, <i>anni.</i>
-Eat with us, Elan.

1713
01:34:35,500 --> 01:34:36,791
She'll be home. I have to cook.

1714
01:34:36,875 --> 01:34:37,833
Cook?

1715
01:34:39,166 --> 01:34:40,833
-Hi, sweethearts!
-Are you cooking?

1716
01:34:41,416 --> 01:34:43,125
-For me?
-It's all for you.

1717
01:34:43,208 --> 01:34:45,291
How sweet!
Best husband ever.

1718
01:34:46,125 --> 01:34:48,125
<i>Even the little leaves</i>

1719
01:34:48,208 --> 01:34:49,958
<i>That drifts along a stream</i>

1720
01:34:50,041 --> 01:34:54,666
<i>Find their way to the shore through</i>
<i>Countless gentle collisions</i>

1721
01:34:54,750 --> 01:34:59,291
<i>When one path comes to an end</i>
<i>A new path begins to unfold</i>

1722
01:34:59,375 --> 01:35:03,541
<i>Slowly, the dawn begins to break</i>

1723
01:35:03,625 --> 01:35:09,208
<i>Nothing lasts forever</i>
<i>Let's live and move forward</i>

1724
01:35:09,291 --> 01:35:12,166
<i>Let us find love before we go</i>

1725
01:35:12,250 --> 01:35:14,166
<i>As the years drift toward the horizon</i>

1726
01:35:14,250 --> 01:35:18,000
<i>Where are we bound?</i>

1727
01:35:18,083 --> 01:35:20,458
<i>Let us just carry love with us</i>

1728
01:35:20,541 --> 01:35:23,083
<i>The wave that touches is also love</i>

1729
01:35:23,166 --> 01:35:25,083
Come here.

1730
01:35:25,166 --> 01:35:27,416
-What?
-Come on. It's okay, sit here.

1731
01:35:29,875 --> 01:35:33,583
I have made a special dosa for you.

1732
01:35:35,041 --> 01:35:37,166
-Have it.
-Okay.

1733
01:35:42,083 --> 01:35:45,583
I make crispy dosa to all.

1734
01:35:45,666 --> 01:35:48,500
But, by the time

1735
01:35:48,583 --> 01:35:50,000
I get ready to eat,

1736
01:35:50,083 --> 01:35:52,500
after setting up the table and all that,

1737
01:35:52,583 --> 01:35:56,166
it will become cold and soggy.

1738
01:36:00,916 --> 01:36:04,916
The last time I ate a crispy dosa
was before my marriage.

1739
01:36:05,000 --> 01:36:07,250
<i>Athai,</i> are you married?

1740
01:36:11,291 --> 01:36:15,625
Honestly, you don't look like that.
You look like Pavi's younger <i>akka.</i>

1741
01:36:30,166 --> 01:36:34,416
<i>Amma,</i> when did you come?
Can't you inform before coming?

1742
01:36:34,500 --> 01:36:38,333
No one is here now, you know?
Can't you inform before coming?

1743
01:36:38,416 --> 01:36:40,500
Wait here.
Let me finish this work and come.

1744
01:36:41,333 --> 01:36:45,666
How are the kids? It's been a long time
since I spoke to <i>anni.</i>

1745
01:36:58,416 --> 01:36:59,458
I'll be right there.

1746
01:37:07,250 --> 01:37:11,000
<i>Amma,</i> can I make a coffee for you?
Wait, I'll come.

1747
01:37:12,958 --> 01:37:14,458
Have this.

1748
01:37:17,916 --> 01:37:19,458
What am I seeing?

1749
01:37:20,250 --> 01:37:22,750
What are you looking at?
Have the coffee.

1750
01:37:22,833 --> 01:37:24,416
Change the dress first.

1751
01:37:28,541 --> 01:37:30,875
What nonsense is this?

1752
01:37:30,958 --> 01:37:33,666
We're having a hard time
worrying about you.

1753
01:37:33,750 --> 01:37:35,916
Have you thought about that?

1754
01:37:37,791 --> 01:37:41,791
Your <i>appa</i> went out of his way
and got a job for you.

1755
01:37:41,875 --> 01:37:44,625
I'm here to share that news with you.

1756
01:37:45,666 --> 01:37:48,625
Go to work properly
and just be like normal people.

1757
01:38:07,833 --> 01:38:11,083
I got a raise. 35,000.

1758
01:38:14,750 --> 01:38:16,125
I too got a job.

1759
01:38:17,041 --> 01:38:19,833
-Congrats.
-25,000 salary.

1760
01:38:21,958 --> 01:38:23,708
I have to start from Monday.

1761
01:38:31,041 --> 01:38:32,916
-Chinnu.
-Yeah?

1762
01:38:33,708 --> 01:38:36,833
Do you really need
to take up a job with such low pay?

1763
01:38:38,875 --> 01:38:45,041
You take such good care of <i>Amma, Appa,</i>
and <i>thatha</i> while you're at home.

1764
01:38:46,333 --> 01:38:49,875
I feel so secure, you know?

1765
01:38:53,750 --> 01:38:58,750
Is there a need that the family will run
only if you go to this job?

1766
01:39:02,458 --> 01:39:06,625
You deserve a much better job, Elan.

1767
01:39:10,666 --> 01:39:16,958
But if you are okay with this,
I don't want to stop you.

1768
01:39:32,791 --> 01:39:34,416
<i>-Amma.</i>
-Elan.

1769
01:39:35,958 --> 01:39:38,791
I hope you are starting
the job from Monday?

1770
01:39:41,958 --> 01:39:44,083
No, <i>Amma,</i> me and Pavi
discussed about this.

1771
01:39:44,666 --> 01:39:46,416
This job won't suit me.

1772
01:39:46,500 --> 01:39:47,833
<i>Convince</i> Appa, <i>please.</i>

1773
01:39:47,916 --> 01:39:50,500
Okay, dear. I will take care.

1774
01:39:57,708 --> 01:40:00,833
He will join for sure. I will see to that.

1775
01:40:06,333 --> 01:40:07,541
Get the vehicle, now.

1776
01:40:17,000 --> 01:40:18,375
You come by car.

1777
01:40:33,708 --> 01:40:35,833
Can't you bring her early?

1778
01:40:35,916 --> 01:40:39,125
Don't you know that regular
health checkups are a must at this age?

1779
01:40:39,208 --> 01:40:40,708
Uncle, I'm asking you only.

1780
01:40:40,791 --> 01:40:44,083
Man, just spit the fact out.

1781
01:40:44,625 --> 01:40:47,666
Seven blockages. It's a complicated case.

1782
01:40:47,750 --> 01:40:49,083
Seven blockages?

1783
01:40:49,166 --> 01:40:52,166
So, open-heart surgery
is needed right away?

1784
01:40:52,250 --> 01:40:54,000
Are you a doctor? Tell me?

1785
01:40:55,333 --> 01:40:56,541
What did the doctor say?

1786
01:40:58,166 --> 01:41:00,000
Doctor, is everything fine?

1787
01:41:00,833 --> 01:41:04,875
<i>Mummy,</i> your daughter-in-law is no joke.
Her arguments are spot on, right?

1788
01:41:04,958 --> 01:41:08,041
Man, she's really going to tear into you.

1789
01:41:08,125 --> 01:41:09,708
What, did she figure it out?

1790
01:41:09,791 --> 01:41:12,500
I had a tough time managing her.

1791
01:41:14,375 --> 01:41:18,125
Why are you stressing out?
Let us hold it for some more time.

1792
01:41:18,208 --> 01:41:21,375
Soon she will stop thinking.
Come on, let's play Uno.

1793
01:41:29,166 --> 01:41:33,458
Michael, Its time. Bring them in.

1794
01:41:34,041 --> 01:41:35,375
Okay. Are you ready, mummy?

1795
01:41:37,833 --> 01:41:40,125
You're just eating peanuts
and acting so much?

1796
01:41:41,041 --> 01:41:42,291
Don't overdo it.

1797
01:41:42,375 --> 01:41:43,708
You got the treatment

1798
01:41:43,791 --> 01:41:45,958
and now you are stable.
Just stick to the script.

1799
01:41:46,041 --> 01:41:48,791
-Enough?
-Actor Savitri is no more. So?

1800
01:41:48,875 --> 01:41:50,291
Go.

1801
01:41:50,375 --> 01:41:53,125
Michael, ensure my husband is not coming.

1802
01:41:53,208 --> 01:41:56,666
He'll read it right off my face.
Send him to the pharmacy for something.

1803
01:41:56,750 --> 01:41:58,958
-Right.
-He's never done anything for me so far.

1804
01:42:01,500 --> 01:42:03,166
She's a little more stable now.

1805
01:42:04,458 --> 01:42:07,000
Let's wait and see.

1806
01:42:07,083 --> 01:42:08,958
Not everyone can go inside.

1807
01:42:09,500 --> 01:42:11,791
Only two important family members
can go in to see her.

1808
01:42:11,875 --> 01:42:13,291
Hello, where are you going?

1809
01:42:14,083 --> 01:42:16,083
I want to see her.

1810
01:42:16,166 --> 01:42:17,958
You go and buy this medicine first.

1811
01:42:18,041 --> 01:42:19,916
You two, go and visit her.

1812
01:42:22,916 --> 01:42:24,958
You can get that only in Tambaram.
Be quick.

1813
01:42:25,041 --> 01:42:27,166
Yes, Tambaram or Thanjavur.
Get it quickly.

1814
01:42:27,250 --> 01:42:28,791
Hi, Vinoth Uncle.

1815
01:42:29,916 --> 01:42:31,333
I'm not Vinoth.

1816
01:42:31,416 --> 01:42:33,166
I'm Dr. Sithar Bootham, okay?

1817
01:42:33,250 --> 01:42:35,583
Yeah, you do look like a goblin. Carry on.

1818
01:42:36,750 --> 01:42:39,500
Growing up just like <i>thatha.</i>
Little devils.

1819
01:42:40,416 --> 01:42:42,500
I got scared, son,

1820
01:42:44,666 --> 01:42:47,916
about whether I'd be able
to see you all again.

1821
01:42:48,750 --> 01:42:51,916
I never expected I'd get a heart attack.

1822
01:42:52,541 --> 01:42:55,666
Why is all this happening
only to our family?

1823
01:42:57,083 --> 01:43:01,250
Elan, please, be outside for a while.

1824
01:43:04,791 --> 01:43:05,791
Go.

1825
01:43:13,708 --> 01:43:14,708
Pavi.

1826
01:43:17,958 --> 01:43:21,166
I was losing my mind
without you and Elan staying with us.

1827
01:43:22,416 --> 01:43:24,208
I have only one desire left.

1828
01:43:24,291 --> 01:43:26,708
Can I ask you something like my daughter?

1829
01:43:26,791 --> 01:43:28,041
Please.

1830
01:43:28,125 --> 01:43:30,500
I just wish I could stay with you all.

1831
01:43:32,208 --> 01:43:34,708
I don't know how long I will survive.

1832
01:43:36,875 --> 01:43:39,208
Can you stay with us for a few days?

1833
01:43:45,416 --> 01:43:46,958
<i>Mummy</i>

1834
01:43:47,041 --> 01:43:50,125
<i>Forget it, she is destined to</i>

1835
01:43:50,916 --> 01:43:54,375
I heard you opted to work from home.

1836
01:43:54,458 --> 01:43:57,125
He said your raise was revoked too.

1837
01:43:57,208 --> 01:43:59,083
Am I troubling you too much?

1838
01:43:59,166 --> 01:44:03,208
No, aunty, don't you worry about that.
Take care of your health first.

1839
01:44:03,291 --> 01:44:04,625
That's the priority.

1840
01:44:06,875 --> 01:44:10,250
Son, why don't you join the job
your <i>appa</i> suggested?

1841
01:44:10,333 --> 01:44:13,791
With extra earning,
Pavi will get some relief from her burden.

1842
01:44:14,500 --> 01:44:16,333
What are you thinking about?

1843
01:44:16,416 --> 01:44:21,041
Now I have two daughters-in-law
who are like my own daughters.

1844
01:44:21,125 --> 01:44:24,500
Pavi, tell him.
He will listen to you only.

1845
01:44:24,583 --> 01:44:25,541
<i>…O-flex, oh, no</i>

1846
01:44:25,625 --> 01:44:28,666
<i>Flex-o-flex, flex-o-flex</i>
<i>Mummy</i>

1847
01:44:28,750 --> 01:44:31,750
<i>Drama, drama, drama queen</i>
<i>Enough overacting now</i>

1848
01:44:31,833 --> 01:44:37,083
<i>You have overtaken our watermelon star</i>
<i>Your performance exceeds reel after reel</i>

1849
01:44:41,416 --> 01:44:44,250
<i>If you scold her, that's it</i>
<i>She's from the con girl batch</i>

1850
01:44:44,333 --> 01:44:47,125
<i>She's devising a plan</i>
<i>My my</i>

1851
01:44:47,208 --> 01:44:50,166
<i>Pal's fallen, very stylish, man</i>

1852
01:44:50,250 --> 01:44:53,333
<i>She would not even stand a Vicks tablet</i>

1853
01:44:53,416 --> 01:44:59,625
<i>Flex-o-flex, flex-o-flex</i>
<i>Oh no, flex-o-flex, flex-o-flex</i>

1854
01:45:26,125 --> 01:45:30,750
<i>Flex-o-flex, oh no!</i>
<i>Flex-o-flex, flex-o-flex</i>

1855
01:45:30,833 --> 01:45:36,541
<i>Flex-o-flex, flex-o-flex, oh no!</i>
<i>Flex-o-flex, flex-o-flex</i>

1856
01:45:36,625 --> 01:45:39,500
<i>She got caught</i>
<i>While trying to set things up while single</i>

1857
01:45:39,583 --> 01:45:42,791
<i>Just checking the vibe</i>
<i>And now she's trapped at home</i>

1858
01:45:42,875 --> 01:45:46,041
<i>Hey! A real-life Squid Game has begun</i>

1859
01:45:46,125 --> 01:45:48,958
<i>Tug-of-war now is getting intense</i>

1860
01:45:49,041 --> 01:45:52,250
<i>Planted a seed, planted a seed</i>

1861
01:45:52,750 --> 01:45:54,250
<i>Enough is enough, Pavi.</i>

1862
01:45:54,333 --> 01:45:56,625
<i>We have decided to downsize the company.</i>

1863
01:45:56,708 --> 01:45:58,708
<i>We need full time employees only.</i>

1864
01:45:58,791 --> 01:45:59,666
<i>Good luck.</i>

1865
01:45:59,750 --> 01:46:01,166
<i>Mummy has won!</i>

1866
01:46:01,250 --> 01:46:02,958
Spider-Man!

1867
01:46:03,041 --> 01:46:04,583
Hey, hey.

1868
01:46:04,666 --> 01:46:06,458
-What happened?
-Nothing.

1869
01:46:06,541 --> 01:46:08,208
Escape.

1870
01:46:13,375 --> 01:46:15,375
Michael, Michael.

1871
01:46:16,041 --> 01:46:18,125
Can I see aunty's medical reports?

1872
01:46:18,208 --> 01:46:21,166
Ashiq's <i>appa</i> is a cardiologist.
We can go for a second opinion.

1873
01:46:22,333 --> 01:46:23,625
You need the reports?

1874
01:46:24,375 --> 01:46:25,583
I'll get them printed.

1875
01:46:28,083 --> 01:46:29,333
What to do now?

1876
01:46:31,250 --> 01:46:32,291
Hands please.

1877
01:46:34,333 --> 01:46:36,458
How is the work?
Is the work load heavy?

1878
01:46:36,541 --> 01:46:38,291
I got used to it now.

1879
01:46:44,666 --> 01:46:48,000
<i>Mummy, the fake reports are all set.</i>

1880
01:46:48,083 --> 01:46:50,333
<i>You just maintain your act.</i>

1881
01:46:50,416 --> 01:46:52,750
<i>Be careful now,</i>
<i>or else she will figure it out.</i>

1882
01:46:52,833 --> 01:46:54,166
<i>Bye, mummy.</i>

1883
01:46:54,250 --> 01:46:56,000
<i>Delete this voice note immediately.</i>

1884
01:46:58,416 --> 01:47:00,083
God. Leave me out of this.

1885
01:47:06,416 --> 01:47:07,875
<i>Amma,</i> what is this?

1886
01:47:09,916 --> 01:47:13,000
I thought you will leave us, <i>Amma.</i>
You scared me.

1887
01:47:13,083 --> 01:47:15,666
You left me already, dear.

1888
01:47:16,791 --> 01:47:20,541
Without you here,
I was only a living corpse.

1889
01:47:24,250 --> 01:47:29,500
In your search for a good life,
you left me behind.

1890
01:47:34,083 --> 01:47:36,958
Even you never thought about me, son.

1891
01:47:37,041 --> 01:47:38,041
Please stop, aunty.

1892
01:47:42,833 --> 01:47:44,791
I treated you like my <i>amma.</i>

1893
01:47:46,083 --> 01:47:47,875
And all of you were pretending.

1894
01:47:51,583 --> 01:47:54,125
No one has ever fooled me like this.

1895
01:47:58,041 --> 01:47:59,916
You hurt me, aunty.

1896
01:48:04,583 --> 01:48:06,541
I didn't expect you would stoop so low.

1897
01:48:10,958 --> 01:48:12,541
Elan, let's go from here.

1898
01:48:17,291 --> 01:48:18,541
Please.

1899
01:48:19,666 --> 01:48:21,750
Please, stay here.

1900
01:48:21,833 --> 01:48:24,875
Please don't leave me.
I will be shattered.

1901
01:48:24,958 --> 01:48:27,208
Please don't go.

1902
01:48:28,583 --> 01:48:30,458
You played
the exact same drama with me too.

1903
01:48:33,708 --> 01:48:35,625
<i>Amma's</i> love is the purest.

1904
01:48:36,375 --> 01:48:38,250
But if you faked that,

1905
01:48:40,291 --> 01:48:41,875
what kind of <i>amma</i> you are?

1906
01:48:46,625 --> 01:48:47,625
Elan, let's leave.

1907
01:48:47,708 --> 01:48:48,958
She is my <i>amma.</i>

1908
01:48:53,500 --> 01:48:54,958
My <i>amma.</i>

1909
01:48:58,291 --> 01:48:59,625
Say sorry to her first.

1910
01:49:01,666 --> 01:49:03,458
Your <i>amma </i>has to apologise. Not me.

1911
01:49:06,166 --> 01:49:09,375
My <i>amma</i> has never spoken ill of you
since we got married.

1912
01:49:10,833 --> 01:49:13,041
Because I never did anything wrong.

1913
01:49:14,166 --> 01:49:17,625
If you have a reason for everything,
then my <i>amma</i> must have her reasons too.

1914
01:49:20,125 --> 01:49:21,333
What justification?

1915
01:49:22,666 --> 01:49:23,875
What justification?

1916
01:49:24,750 --> 01:49:26,416
Forcing me to leave my job?

1917
01:49:27,416 --> 01:49:31,125
Or separating me from my <i>amma</i> and <i>appa?</i>

1918
01:49:32,541 --> 01:49:34,916
I also came to your house
leaving my family. Understand it.

1919
01:49:35,000 --> 01:49:38,416
Elan, I never lied
or tricked you to my house.

1920
01:49:39,291 --> 01:49:41,291
I told the truth and called you.

1921
01:49:44,666 --> 01:49:46,625
We're not going to force you to stay here.

1922
01:49:47,833 --> 01:49:48,958
You can leave if you want.

1923
01:49:53,708 --> 01:49:56,375
Elan, if I leave now, I will not return.

1924
01:50:00,000 --> 01:50:02,875
If you leave now,
don't expect me to follow, Pavi.

1925
01:50:12,625 --> 01:50:13,958
Pavi…

1926
01:50:14,958 --> 01:50:20,125
<i>Hey lady</i>

1927
01:50:20,208 --> 01:50:26,833
<i>You're taking my heart along</i>

1928
01:50:26,916 --> 01:50:31,125
<i>My love</i>

1929
01:50:32,125 --> 01:50:38,375
<i>You're killing my love as you walk away</i>

1930
01:50:41,541 --> 01:50:43,208
DAD - UNCLE - AUNTY

1931
01:50:43,291 --> 01:50:47,000
<i>Hey, my pains</i>

1932
01:50:47,083 --> 01:50:53,958
<i>You keep wounding me</i>

1933
01:50:54,041 --> 01:50:58,250
{\an8}<i>Tell me, love</i>

1934
01:50:58,333 --> 01:51:04,958
{\an8}<i>I see my dreams getting shattered</i>

1935
01:51:06,000 --> 01:51:08,791
<i>Pyaar, prema, kaadhal</i>

1936
01:51:08,875 --> 01:51:11,750
<i>Pyaar, prema, kaadhal</i>

1937
01:51:11,833 --> 01:51:14,666
<i>Pyaar, prema, kaadhal</i>

1938
01:51:14,750 --> 01:51:17,375
<i>Pyaar, prema, kaadhal</i>

1939
01:51:18,916 --> 01:51:21,500
<i>Now a days, he comes home very late.</i>

1940
01:51:23,375 --> 01:51:25,041
What did I do wrong?

1941
01:51:25,791 --> 01:51:28,541
My son has suffered so much
at their house.

1942
01:51:30,875 --> 01:51:33,541
I don't think it will work out.

1943
01:51:35,166 --> 01:51:39,208
I think it is best for them both
to part ways.

1944
01:51:39,291 --> 01:51:43,333
The hardship you mention is what I've been
doing here for the past ten years.

1945
01:51:44,083 --> 01:51:45,541
What's so hard about it?

1946
01:51:46,833 --> 01:51:50,125
My husband goes out to work
for the family's sake.

1947
01:51:50,208 --> 01:51:52,500
I labour inside the house
for the same family.

1948
01:51:53,166 --> 01:51:56,250
Is there any rule that says who should
stay at home and who should go to work?

1949
01:51:57,625 --> 01:52:01,500
You want them to part ways because
you think your son is having a hard time.

1950
01:52:01,583 --> 01:52:05,000
If my <i>amma</i> thought like that,
what would've happened to us?

1951
01:52:12,458 --> 01:52:13,833
It's jaggery coffee.

1952
01:52:29,500 --> 01:52:33,291
I'm not doing this because you like it.

1953
01:52:33,375 --> 01:52:35,458
I do this because I like you.

1954
01:52:35,541 --> 01:52:40,583
What? If I'm tired after doing chores,
won't you press my feet?

1955
01:52:41,333 --> 01:52:42,708
Have your coffee.

1956
01:52:43,791 --> 01:52:46,041
<i>Love</i>

1957
01:52:46,125 --> 01:52:47,791
<i>Is my love</i>

1958
01:52:49,583 --> 01:52:53,583
<i>Meant to be forgotten</i>

1959
01:52:55,208 --> 01:53:01,250
<i>You one word kills me</i>
<i>Like a death sentence</i>

1960
01:53:01,333 --> 01:53:07,250
<i>I have no words left to say</i>
<i>The silence grows longer</i>

1961
01:53:07,333 --> 01:53:13,208
<i>Do not walk away</i>
<i>Lady'll be left alone</i>

1962
01:53:13,291 --> 01:53:15,708
<i>I'd ask another birth…</i>

1963
01:53:15,791 --> 01:53:17,666
Pavi, haven't you slept yet?

1964
01:53:17,750 --> 01:53:20,208
<i>…to be with you</i>

1965
01:53:20,291 --> 01:53:23,583
You thought you will change the system,

1966
01:53:23,666 --> 01:53:27,458
but unknowingly
you also started following the same.

1967
01:53:28,375 --> 01:53:31,833
If a man says a woman
doesn't need to work

1968
01:53:31,916 --> 01:53:36,166
is considered male chauvinism,
then what are you doing?

1969
01:53:37,833 --> 01:53:40,958
It doesn't have a name, right?
Think about it.

1970
01:53:44,791 --> 01:53:47,666
<i>Pyaar, prema, kaadhal</i>

1971
01:53:47,750 --> 01:53:50,583
<i>Pyaar, prema, kaadhal</i>

1972
01:53:50,666 --> 01:53:53,666
<i>Pyaar, prema, kaadhal</i>

1973
01:53:53,750 --> 01:53:56,583
<i>Pyaar, prema, kaadhal</i>

1974
01:53:58,541 --> 01:54:00,750
I hate you

1975
01:54:00,833 --> 01:54:02,750
and Elan too.

1976
01:54:02,833 --> 01:54:05,458
I like it when you two are together.

1977
01:54:09,166 --> 01:54:13,375
If you'd gone to live with your husband
after marriage like other girls,

1978
01:54:14,333 --> 01:54:16,041
I wouldn't have felt bad.

1979
01:54:16,916 --> 01:54:19,208
Because every <i>amma</i> knows

1980
01:54:19,291 --> 01:54:21,833
that her daughter will move out one day.

1981
01:54:23,375 --> 01:54:28,125
But the groom's parents
wouldn't have thought that way.

1982
01:54:28,208 --> 01:54:33,291
Had I been in their place,
I would not let him go with you.

1983
01:54:35,083 --> 01:54:37,041
You may not understand it now.

1984
01:54:37,916 --> 01:54:40,208
When you become a mother,
you'll understand.

1985
01:54:43,583 --> 01:54:46,291
We didn't get you married
to the girl you love

1986
01:54:46,375 --> 01:54:48,791
to watch you
and our family suffer like this.

1987
01:54:50,708 --> 01:54:54,791
Looking at things, I now fear
your <i>amma</i> may get a real heart attack.

1988
01:54:56,666 --> 01:54:59,791
Your decisions against me
have never really worked out.

1989
01:55:02,041 --> 01:55:03,791
Listen to me at least from now on.

1990
01:55:06,791 --> 01:55:08,416
Get married again.

1991
01:55:09,583 --> 01:55:13,000
<i>-Appa,</i> I don't want to--
-Enough.

1992
01:55:13,083 --> 01:55:15,375
I'll make the right decision for you.

1993
01:55:28,375 --> 01:55:32,208
If you move with us,
your parents will suffer.

1994
01:55:33,625 --> 01:55:37,583
If I move in with them, I will suffer.

1995
01:55:42,666 --> 01:55:46,708
I wish we had never even met here.

1996
01:55:53,500 --> 01:55:57,875
Do what makes your family happy.

1997
01:56:18,458 --> 01:56:22,041
<i>What have you done</i>
<i>You crushed my heart</i>

1998
01:56:22,125 --> 01:56:24,750
<i>Cajole me a little</i>
<i>And tell me your love</i>

1999
01:56:24,833 --> 01:56:27,291
<i>You are the sky</i>
<i>You are the earth</i>

2000
01:56:27,375 --> 01:56:29,875
<i>You are my life, lady</i>

2001
01:56:29,958 --> 01:56:34,708
<i>Even if you chase me</i>
<i>I wouldn't go…</i>

2002
01:56:34,791 --> 01:56:37,291
I feel sorry for your friend.

2003
01:56:37,375 --> 01:56:38,708
<i>…I'm seeing love…</i>

2004
01:56:38,791 --> 01:56:42,916
Not only him.
You are also suffering with me.

2005
01:56:43,000 --> 01:56:44,791
Don't be naughty.

2006
01:56:45,291 --> 01:56:47,791
Can we go for a Thailand trip?

2007
01:56:47,875 --> 01:56:48,916
Love you, dear.

2008
01:56:49,000 --> 01:56:52,416
Baby, we're meant to
get married just once, right?

2009
01:56:52,500 --> 01:56:54,458
It's in your hand, baby.

2010
01:56:55,375 --> 01:56:57,375
Hi, sweethearts.

2011
01:56:57,458 --> 01:57:01,250
Now you are watching the second marriage

2012
01:57:01,333 --> 01:57:03,166
of our favourite influencer

2013
01:57:03,250 --> 01:57:04,666
Purple Pavi's ex-husband,

2014
01:57:04,750 --> 01:57:06,291
live from here.

2015
01:57:06,375 --> 01:57:08,958
Are you ready?
It's party time.

2016
01:57:10,875 --> 01:57:15,333
Nirmala, is it finally turning out
the way I wanted?

2017
01:57:15,416 --> 01:57:17,666
Bring the bride please.

2018
01:57:22,333 --> 01:57:23,416
Chinnu.

2019
01:57:38,958 --> 01:57:40,291
What?

2020
01:57:40,375 --> 01:57:41,500
What are you staring at?

2021
01:57:42,291 --> 01:57:44,500
Stop portraying your <i>appa</i> as a villain.

2022
01:57:44,583 --> 01:57:46,500
I was your age once. I faced it.

2023
01:57:46,583 --> 01:57:50,583
I was acting strict because
I wanted you to become responsible.

2024
01:57:50,666 --> 01:57:54,208
The minute you went to
Pavi's house, you proved it.

2025
01:57:54,791 --> 01:57:57,250
Thank her first.

2026
01:58:02,708 --> 01:58:06,041
The other day, I said too much
in the heat of the moment.

2027
01:58:06,791 --> 01:58:07,791
Sorry.

2028
01:58:08,375 --> 01:58:12,666
Nobody finds it odd when a woman
moves into her husband's house.

2029
01:58:13,708 --> 01:58:18,208
But everyone finds it odd when a man
moves into his wife's house.

2030
01:58:19,375 --> 01:58:21,791
In the process of finding an answer,

2031
01:58:23,750 --> 01:58:25,208
I don't want to lose the one I love.

2032
01:58:26,583 --> 01:58:29,750
Elan loves you all.

2033
01:58:29,833 --> 01:58:30,958
Despite that,

2034
01:58:32,250 --> 01:58:36,208
he left everything behind to live
in my house because of his love for me.

2035
01:58:39,208 --> 01:58:44,750
Now I'm going to do this
to prove my love for him.

2036
01:58:46,833 --> 01:58:49,541
-I will move in with you all.
-You go home.

2037
01:58:51,416 --> 01:58:54,083
This time, I will come
and invite you traditionally.

2038
01:58:55,666 --> 01:58:58,791
You both married earlier against my wish.

2039
01:58:58,875 --> 01:59:01,125
Now let the same thing
happen with my blessings.

2040
01:59:01,208 --> 01:59:02,291
Tie the knot.

2041
01:59:03,208 --> 01:59:04,750
Tie the knot!

2042
01:59:06,500 --> 01:59:08,541
-She has one already.
-How many knots you put then?

2043
01:59:08,625 --> 01:59:10,833
-Three.
-Do you know the meaning of those?

2044
01:59:11,708 --> 01:59:15,083
The first knot signifies
that the couple must care for each other.

2045
01:59:15,166 --> 01:59:19,833
The second signifies that both families
should support one another.

2046
01:59:19,916 --> 01:59:21,291
The third knot signifies that

2047
01:59:21,375 --> 01:59:24,041
the groom's family must take
good care of the bride.

2048
01:59:24,125 --> 01:59:25,666
Now the fourth.

2049
01:59:25,750 --> 01:59:29,500
If the groom moves in
with the bride's family,

2050
01:59:29,583 --> 01:59:31,208
they should take good care of him.

2051
01:59:31,291 --> 01:59:32,291
Super.

2052
01:59:32,375 --> 01:59:33,500
I'll tie it now!

2053
01:59:37,625 --> 01:59:39,875
Apply the vermilion too.

2054
01:59:52,916 --> 01:59:54,500
"Are you okay, Ammu?

2055
01:59:57,333 --> 02:00:00,333
-Boss, take that right.
-App shows straight, sir.

2056
02:00:00,416 --> 02:00:01,458
I'm on the right route.

2057
02:00:01,541 --> 02:00:03,583
Don't I know the way to my home?
Take the right.

2058
02:00:03,666 --> 02:00:07,541
You <i>appa</i> told me not to listen to you.
He asked me to follow the map.

2059
02:00:12,833 --> 02:00:14,708
Dear, come inside.

2060
02:00:15,416 --> 02:00:16,625
Come.

2061
02:00:18,000 --> 02:00:19,041
Come in.

2062
02:00:23,958 --> 02:00:26,083
This is where you are going to live.

2063
02:00:26,708 --> 02:00:29,083
A new house bought for your wedding.

2064
02:00:29,166 --> 02:00:32,291
Our old house is small for our big family.

2065
02:00:32,375 --> 02:00:34,291
What you said the other day
was right, dear.

2066
02:00:34,375 --> 02:00:38,708
Showering love on one's own child alone
will not make a good <i>amma.</i>

2067
02:00:39,916 --> 02:00:43,791
You are no different to me from Elan.

2068
02:00:43,875 --> 02:00:47,041
We do not intend you
to leave your parents.

2069
02:00:47,583 --> 02:00:49,000
Come, come.

2070
02:00:49,083 --> 02:00:51,125
Here we are all going to live together.

2071
02:00:51,208 --> 02:00:52,291
Come.

2072
02:01:00,958 --> 02:01:03,083
PYAAR, PREMA, KAADHAL HOUSE

2073
02:01:03,166 --> 02:01:06,708
{\an8}<i>Wow. This is something new.</i>

2074
02:01:06,791 --> 02:01:08,625
{\an8}<i>Super ending.</i>

2075
02:01:08,708 --> 02:01:11,958
{\an8}<i>What is new in this?</i>
<i>Joint families have been around for ages!</i>

2076
02:01:12,041 --> 02:01:14,208
{\an8}<i>Do you know what a joint family is?</i>

2077
02:01:14,291 --> 02:01:18,916
{\an8}<i>It's about the bride alone joining</i>
<i>the groom's extended family.</i>

2078
02:01:19,000 --> 02:01:20,333
{\an8}<i>Got it?</i>

2079
02:01:20,416 --> 02:01:25,416
{\an8}<i>Gosh! From now on,</i>
<i>every girl will demand this, right?</i>

2080
02:01:25,500 --> 02:01:27,500
{\an8}<i>Who on earth came up with this?</i>

2081
02:01:50,458 --> 02:01:54,166
Thief, catch him!

2082
02:01:54,250 --> 02:01:56,666
-See, he is there.
-Where?

2083
02:01:56,750 --> 02:01:59,250
-He jumped over and is running off.
-Where did these two disappear?

2084
02:01:59,333 --> 02:02:02,833
Run fast.
Let's escape from their torture.

2085
02:02:04,125 --> 02:02:07,583
-Chinnu.
-Who will give the medicines to your <i>appa?</i>

2086
02:02:07,666 --> 02:02:10,666
-Don't worry. <i>Amma</i> will take care.
-Okay.

2087
02:02:10,750 --> 02:02:13,041
-If your <i>amma</i> falls sick?
-My <i>appa</i> will take care.

2088
02:02:13,125 --> 02:02:17,750
Let us worry about our life first.
They trouble us a lot.

2089
02:02:17,833 --> 02:02:22,500
Instead, you and I can torture each other.
Run fast, else they'll catch us.

2090
02:05:12,000 --> 02:05:17,000
Subtitle translation by: Shobana Raju,
Venkat Krishnamachari, Sobana Sundar